SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Exeter Arts and Culture: Arts Commission 20
 26/27 (organisational cultures and narrative infrastructure)
DESCRIPTION:The University of Exeter's annual flagship Arts Commission invi
 tes a creative practitioner in any artform interested in organisational cu
 ltures (how people work together in formal settings\, and how those cultur
 es can be disrupted\, adjusted and reimagined) to work with academics in t
 he Faculty of Humanities\, Arts and Social Sciences.\n\nOrganisation: Univ
 ersity of Exeter Arts and Culture\, with the Faculty of Humanities\, Arts 
 and Social Sciences (HASS)\nLocation: Exeter\, UK (Streatham campus\, with
  some activity possible at Penryn\, Cornwall). Minimum two days a month in
  person and online\, January to June 2027. No nationality or residence res
 triction stated.\nAward: Artist fee GBP 14\,000 (incl. VAT\, also covering
  travel\, subsistence and accommodation) plus a production and presentatio
 n budget of up to GBP 4\,000\; a freelance creative producer is paid separ
 ately. Interviewed candidates receive GBP 100. No application fee.\nDurati
 on: January to July 2027\; artwork completed and presented by end of July 
 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.artsandcultureexeter.co.uk/news/arts-and-cultur
 e-arts-commission-2026-27?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://www.artsandcultureexeter.co.uk/news/arts-and-culture-arts-commi
 ssion-2026-27?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Exeter\, UK (Streatham campus\, with some activity possible at Pen
 ryn\, Cornwall). Minimum two days a month in person and online\, January t
 o June 2027. No nationality or residence restriction stated.
END:VEVENT
